WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.960
(light stately music)

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.157
- [Martin Luther King Jr.] I have a dream.

00:00:06.157 --> 00:00:07.717
- I'm gonna be very honest with you,

00:00:07.717 --> 00:00:09.867
when I do Dr. King and I'm performing,

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:12.446
it's as if Dr. King takes over.

00:00:12.446 --> 00:00:16.507
- Mine eyes have seen the glory
of the coming of the Lord.

00:00:16.507 --> 00:00:20.696
- It's like the spirit of
Dr. King comes into the room.

00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:24.125
- We hold these truths to be self-evident,

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:25.036
that all men
- that all men

00:00:25.036 --> 00:00:27.774
are created equal.
- are created equal.

00:00:27.774 --> 00:00:29.423
- If you listen to the majority

00:00:29.423 --> 00:00:31.125
of his speeches right now,

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:34.115
it's right in line with what
we're dealing with today.

00:00:34.115 --> 00:00:38.665
Free at last, free at
last, thank God almighty

00:00:38.665 --> 00:00:39.745
we are free at last.

00:00:39.745 --> 00:00:41.995
(applause)

00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:47.622
(reflective piano music)

00:00:47.622 --> 00:00:49.902
My name is Stephon Ferguson.

00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:51.454
I travel across the world performing

00:00:51.454 --> 00:00:55.753
as the Reverend Dr.
Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:00:55.753 --> 00:00:58.206
I am the only person who is licensed

00:00:58.206 --> 00:00:59.995
by the King Estate to perform the works

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:00.995
of Dr. King.

00:01:02.715 --> 00:01:04.617
I used to be a deejay.

00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:07.059
We took some of Dr. King's old records

00:01:07.059 --> 00:01:09.601
and as we were mixing them in,

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.861
I began to emulate some of Dr. King's

00:01:11.861 --> 00:01:16.006
old records, particularly I Have a Dream.

00:01:16.006 --> 00:01:17.425
A good friend of mine said,

00:01:17.425 --> 00:01:19.638
"Man, you sound just like Dr. King.

00:01:19.638 --> 00:01:21.849
"You should really consider taking your

00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:23.849
"work to another level."

00:01:24.697 --> 00:01:26.817
I realized that it was a gift

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:29.049
that God had given me to continue

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:32.049
the work and the legacy of Dr. King.

00:01:33.529 --> 00:01:37.747
Let freedom ring from
the prodigious hilltops

00:01:37.747 --> 00:01:41.248
of New Hampshire, let freedom ring.

00:01:41.248 --> 00:01:44.638
I've been performing as Dr.
King for about 15 years.

00:01:44.638 --> 00:01:47.176
I get a lot of requests to perform

00:01:47.176 --> 00:01:50.478
in different areas from Madrid, Spain;

00:01:50.478 --> 00:01:52.438
London, England.

00:01:52.438 --> 00:01:54.907
I've been honored to get recognition

00:01:54.907 --> 00:01:56.849
from a lot of great people.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.718
President Barack Obama reached out to me.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.217
I have a letter thanking me for my work,

00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:05.696
so that was a very powerful recognition.

00:02:05.696 --> 00:02:09.129
I've even got that from
King family members.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.227
(fast-paced piano music)

00:02:12.227 --> 00:02:14.297
- I speak for the entire family

00:02:14.297 --> 00:02:17.736
that we know of no one who can actually

00:02:17.736 --> 00:02:19.403
sound like my uncle.

00:02:21.203 --> 00:02:23.491
- God loves all of his children.

00:02:23.491 --> 00:02:25.243
- His cadence is unique.

00:02:25.243 --> 00:02:27.723
It has a slow, southern drawl to it,

00:02:27.723 --> 00:02:31.461
but a sophistication at the same time.

00:02:31.461 --> 00:02:34.800
And Stephon just really flatters us all

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.731
with the way that he's able to bring

00:02:36.731 --> 00:02:39.231
my uncle's voice back to life.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.490
- I believe it resonates with people

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.152
because we're living in
a time that we need it.

00:02:46.152 --> 00:02:49.032
With all the hatred, the divisiveness,

00:02:49.032 --> 00:02:51.310
the things that we see in the world,

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.520
I think it really inspires people

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.687
to stand up, to speak out.

00:02:58.029 --> 00:03:02.086
I may get to the age where
it's gonna be difficult,

00:03:02.086 --> 00:03:04.919
but I'll still be trying to do it.

